# Further Research

These definitions of directedness and boundary families inspire a flurry of research topics and generalizations. For one, going back to the original inspirations behind these, we generate a couple new classes that we can try to find the generating functions of. Some, like [wings](/classes/wing) and [crescents](/classes/crescent), should be feasible using existing methods, while others, like [trees](/classes/tree) [bent trees](/classes/bent-tree) might require more work.

In particular, directedness classes relate in interesting ways in the other candidates for classification that we discussed in the first part.

